stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> RAISED: C1 tenant, operator or a portal rejection raises a claim
    RAISED --> TRIAGED: C2 covered obligation and covered period confirmed
    RAISED --> OUT_OF_SCOPE: C3 obligation not in the tenant SLA schedule
    TRIAGED --> EVIDENCE_PENDING: C4 causation record incomplete
    EVIDENCE_PENDING --> TRIAGED: C5 missing artefact supplied
    EVIDENCE_PENDING --> OUT_OF_SCOPE: C6 evidence window lapses
    TRIAGED --> CAUSATION_REVIEW: C7 causation record complete and sealed
    CAUSATION_REVIEW --> ATTRIBUTED_TO_US: C8 defect in our artefact, our schedule or a submission we contracted to make
    CAUSATION_REVIEW --> ATTRIBUTED_TO_CUSTOMER: C9 customer data, customer delay or unremitted funds
    CAUSATION_REVIEW --> ATTRIBUTED_TO_EXTERNAL: C10 portal outage, unreleased format or a carve-out event
    ATTRIBUTED_TO_US --> REMEDIATION: C11 refile, revise or supplement, per the filing machine
    REMEDIATION --> REMEDY_COMPUTED: C12 portal acknowledgement captured
    REMEDY_COMPUTED --> CAPPED: C13 per-incident and annual caps applied
    CAPPED --> SETTLED: C14 credit note issued against the next invoice
    ATTRIBUTED_TO_CUSTOMER --> CLOSED_NO_REMEDY: C15 findings and evidence returned to the tenant
    ATTRIBUTED_TO_EXTERNAL --> CLOSED_NO_REMEDY: C16 carve-out recorded and the fence cross-referenced
    OUT_OF_SCOPE --> CLOSED_NO_REMEDY: C17 closed with reasons
    CLOSED_NO_REMEDY --> DISPUTED: C18 tenant disputes the attribution
    CAPPED --> DISPUTED: C18 tenant disputes the cap
    DISPUTED --> CAUSATION_REVIEW: C19 reopened with new evidence
    DISPUTED --> ESCALATED: C20 escalation to the named commercial owner
    ESCALATED --> SETTLED: C21 settled above or below the computed remedy, with reasons recorded
    ESCALATED --> CLOSED_NO_REMEDY: C22 escalation upholds the attribution
    SETTLED --> [*]
    CLOSED_NO_REMEDY --> [*]

    note left of CAUSATION_REVIEW
      Runs only on the sealed causation record.
      Who supplied the data, when we generated,
      who submitted under which written authority,
      and the acknowledgement identifier.
    end note

    note right of CAPPED
      The remedy is contractual.
      The statutory liability stays with
      the employer and the deductor.
    end note
